course: dictionary
lesson: 11560
title: Analogy: finding the link
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: An analogy is a comparison that explains one thing by showing how it is like another. Scientists use them to make hard ideas easy to picture. «Electricity flows through a wire like water flows through a pipe.» You know how water moves, so that picture helps you understand electricity.
explain: In word puzzles, an analogy is a pair of pairs: «A is to B as C is to D». First find the link in the first pair, then look for the same link in the second pair. «Hot is to cold as up is to down»: hot and cold are opposites, and so are up and down.
explain: You may meet the phrases «draw an analogy», «a good analogy», «by analogy» and «an analogy between». When a writer draws an analogy, they ask you to compare two things and see what they have in common.
fact: An analogy is a comparison that shows how two things are alike in some way.
fact: «The heart is like a pump» is an analogy: the heart pushes blood round the body, just as a pump pushes water along a pipe.
fact: In a word analogy, the link in the first pair must be the same as the link in the second pair.
fact: Common links include opposites (hot and cold), part and whole (wheel and car), and young and adult (puppy and dog).
fact: Analogy can also mean a likeness between two things, such as «an analogy between the brain and a computer».
exercise: «Puppy is to dog as kitten is to ?» | Bark | *Cat | Mouse | Milk
exercise: «Hot is to cold as up is to ?» | Hill | *Down | Sky | Tall
exercise: «Wheel is to car as leaf is to ?» | *Tree | Garden | Green | Autumn
test: «Pen is to write as knife is to ?» | Kitchen | Sharp | *Cut | Metal
test: «Bird is to fly as fish is to ?» | *Swim | Sea | Water | Scales
exam: «Light is to dark as loud is to ?» | *Quiet | Noise | Music | Shout
